# hebrew

// in general, hebrew letters are drawn in print form (high contrast
// between horizontal and vertical segments) and keep their serifs.
// some features should be exaggerated for better readability;
// heels (an extruded end of segments) are usual subjects for this.
//
// alef is the only letter with the prominent (anti)diagonal segment,
// which heavily constrains the design space and every other letter
// follows it. the basic design space is 6x10---smaller than latin's
// 7x10---as result, and should be liberally expanded as such.
//
// TODO: biblical hebrew (cantillation marks + masora marks)

feature ccmp for hebr : anchor he-above
feature ccmp for hebr : anchor he-below align c

